Select the architecture-neutral optimized kernels when RVV is disabled.

ENABLE_RVV exists and defaults to OFF, but the optimized-kernel CMake code
picks the riscv64/ directory purely from CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR. Some files
there use RVV intrinsics directly, including code not fully guarded by
#if __riscv_vector, so a scalar riscv64 build still emits vector instructions
and traps with SIGILL on a core without the V extension.

Gate the riscv64 kernel directory on ENABLE_RVV so a scalar build falls back
to the architecture-neutral optimized implementations (and from there to the
reference kernels as needed).

Upstream: not submitted (local build-configuration change).
Signed-off-by: K230 SDK <dev@example.com>

--- a/src/Native/src/kernels/stackvm/optimized/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/Native/src/kernels/stackvm/optimized/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 cmake_minimum_required (VERSION 3.13)
 
-if(${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} MATCHES "riscv64")
+if(${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} MATCHES "riscv64" AND ENABLE_RVV)
     set(ARCH riscv64)
 elseif(${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} MATCHES "(x86)|(X86)|(amd64)|(AMD64)|(x86_64)|(X86_64)")
     set(ARCH x86_64)
